# Source files are always diffed as TEXT. A single control byte inside a string
# literal (services/chat-service/src/domain.ts held a raw NUL as the dm_key
# separator) makes git classify the whole file as binary and render its diff as
# "Bin 3119 -> 4495 bytes" — unreviewable in a PR. Forcing the `diff` attribute
# keeps review working even if such a literal reappears.
*.ts diff
*.tsx diff
